  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "$3.5-5.5=$",
  "worked_solution": "To subtract $5.5$ from $3.5,$ we break up $5.5$ into its whole number part ($5$) and its decimal part ($0.5$) and proceed in two steps.\n\n- We start at $3.5$ on the number line and move $5$ places to the left, which brings us to $-1.5.$\n\n- Then, we move $0.5$ places to the left, leaving us at $-2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14149078/assets/03bb210af203fe32601f53197d1e14f3e6a5267a495d3eb9b04f4c8c47781f0d.png)\n\n This gives $3.5-5.5=-2.$",
